[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) held every report about a wrong date and called them one issue with
one fix queued. Most of its reports share one cause, the parser, and #4471 stays that ticket. Two
other problems sat inside it, and the queued fix covers neither. Their reports are now merged into
tickets of their own, so each table below counts what its ticket covers.

## parser: #4471

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The shared parser reads every date month first. All our tenants write the day first, so a
booking for 2 March comes out as 3 February. This covers app and email reports from every
tenant, and form reports from tenants on booking-v2.

The [incident page](/kb/incidents/4471) still gives the count from before the split in its text.
Its table is current.

## hint: [#2](https://github.com/dandezmirean/support-kb/issues/2)

<CauseTable ticket={2} />

The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type the month first, as
the hint tells them, and the form reads the date the tenant's way, day first. A parser fix
leaves these broken. The hint has to change. Only tenants on booking-v3 who book through the
form hit it.

## one-day move: [#5](https://github.com/dandezmirean/support-kb/issues/5)

<CauseTable ticket={5} />

These reports have no day and month swapped. The booking lands one day early, or on a different
day depending on where the reader is: "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got
Monday." That points at time zones, not at the parser. The desk's notes read them as a one-day
move. The table still names their cause `parser`, because the cause comes from the tenant and the
channel (`causes.ts`), and these came by app and email from day-first tenants. The note under the
table is the desk's reading.

Intake's tag guesses from the reporter's browser and disagrees with the cause often, so this page
does not use it.

